# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# When this file exists EAS uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore, so everything that should
# stay out of the build archive has to be repeated here.
#
# It exists for one reason: google-services.json is .gitignore'd (it is restored from a
# secret in CI rather than committed), so EAS never received it. `app.config.js` sets
# `android.googleServicesFile` only when that file is present, and @expo/fingerprint
# hashes both the config and the file's contents. The result was two different
# fingerprints -- one on the CI machine that had the file, one on the build worker that
# did not -- and with `runtimeVersion.policy: fingerprint` the build hard-fails with
# "Runtime version calculated on local machine not equal to runtime version calculated
# during build."
#
# The same mismatch would also have silently prevented every OTA update from reaching a
# real build, because expo-updates matches on that fingerprint.
#
# google-services.json is deliberately NOT listed below: it is a client-side Firebase
# config that already ships inside the APK, so uploading it to the builder is safe.
node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
.DS_Store
*.log
.env
.env.local
*.jks
*.keystore
ios/
android/
